# SFT execution status v0.76

2026-09-10. The generated tiny importer now has a dedicated Linux bootstrap,
prepared-rootfs guardian composition, closed source add-on and private source
staging path. This is local software integration, not a native Linux acceptance
run, real-checkpoint import or completion of Gate 5.

No real checkpoint/trainer/tokenizer payloads or datasets were opened. No
network action, dependency installation, Docker, AWS, CI, GPU, inference,
training, instance action or GitHub publication was initiated. Frozen evidence,
the original importer and saved real-import plan remain byte-for-byte unchanged.

## What this stage connects

The versioned source add-on installs only the fixed importer entry, exact
manifest and a closed flat Python source tree into an independently admitted
OwnedRootfs. It checks all pins, bytes, entries and ancestor conflicts before
writing. Files are new O_EXCL/no-follow 0444 copies; the frozen two-path installer
allowlist is unchanged. A started write or freeze failure taints the tree and
cannot be resumed. Source hashing does not establish runtime origin or code safety.

The dedicated child bootstrap attaches to the owned cgroup before importing ML,
installs the frozen loopback-only network namespace, read-only OCI root,
Landlock and narrow IPC filter, drops to uid/gid 10001, closes authority FDs,
then waits for exactly one release byte. It rejects extra bytes, ancillary
data, truncation, extra queued packets and premature EOF. Its environment and
Python executable/arguments are closed; there is no real-input argument.

The composition uses the unchanged SHA-bound controller/guardian fixture in a
fresh isolated module. The guardian owns the cgroup, arms controller-loss and
deadline handling before release, then checks worker exit, one bounded aggregate
packet, EOF, descendant reaping and empty cgroup removal. A failed or ambiguous
kill/close is never retried. This internal API assumes an independently
authenticated, prepared/frozen rootfs and host-side source bundle; it does not
acquire or approve them. Every native entry rejects this Mac before mutation.

The tiny profile is 4 GiB memory, zero swap, 256 pids, two CPU cores' quota and
at most 90 seconds overall; the entry's cooperative budget is 45 seconds and
the importer budget is 30 seconds. The 512 MiB /tmp and 64 MiB /dev/shm tmpfs
limits are simultaneous capacities, not cumulative-write quotas. An independent
outer supervisor remains necessary; guardian death and hostile root are not covered.

## Ownership compatibility fixed without weakening the loader

The original root-owned source code would fail the frozen ContentIO check that
control files belong to the running uid. The fix preserves that check: after
authenticating the exact root-owned tree, the entry writes byte-identical copies
into a fresh uid-10001 private directory, changes only these new files to 0400,
and verifies their bytes again. The original files are never chmodded or chowned.
Only this copied tree is inserted into the import path, with genuine __file__
paths. The original nonempty Lumi initializer and auto-registration semantics
are preserved; no synthetic initializer or fake module path is substituted.

The bound importer closure contains 35 files / 610,752 bytes, within the caps
of 128 files, 256 KiB per file and 4 MiB total. Its manifest cap is 65,536 bytes.
The closure covers static relative imports and the explicit dynamic model/config
roots used by this tiny path. It is not a universal dependency-closure proof.
Source verification, source-copy reservations and readback counts are separate
from the unchanged importer ledger; dependency/module loader I/O is not in it.
Uid-owned 0400 copies are compatible, not immutable against their own owner.

## Local verification

1,146 distinct targeted tests pass with no failures or skips: 1,046 stdlib
tests on Python 3.11.15, 3.13.7 and 3.14.6 (1.855s, 1.869s and 1.896s), plus
100 tiny CPU tests on Python 3.13.7 (2.851s / 4.055s supervised wall time).
The 60-second parent timeout applies to each test process. This includes all
711 v0.75 tests, 340 frozen containment-helper regressions and 95 new tests.
Ruff E,F,I,B,UP / py311 / line length 100 passes on all twelve new code/test files.

The fixed tiny fixture generates a vocab-17, hidden-8, one-layer FP32 DCP source
and converts/packages it through frozen kernel v5 and coordinator/package v2.
It performs one import, two checkpoint audits, two tokenizer audits and the
frozen worker checksum verification. Forward and optimizer calls remain zero.
An isolated subprocess starts without Lumi/ML loaded and runs this chain using
only the exact private source copies. Its genuine aggregate result also passes
the new guardian's strict packet/result validator.

The final aggregate test counts, timings and file bindings are recorded in
`evidence/lumi-4b-sft-import-guard-integration-v0.1.json`; structural verification
is separate. Local tests use pure syscall doubles, tiny generated tar trees and
tiny CPU tensors. They never invoke native namespace, mount, cgroup, privilege
or entry operations. They are not the full repository suite or Linux proof.

The five predecessor reports' 65 binding references (59 unique files; 60 refs
include byte counts) and the saved plan's internal digest are checked. Existing
Torch platform/deprecation and ctypes layout warnings are not hidden or treated
as new native acceptance evidence.

## Remaining boundary, without repeating completed work

The older OCI guardian's Linux CPU acceptance in v0.68 already passed. Its
bounded acquisition/run is not repeated, and its receipt does not qualify this
new importer or new add-on. The accepted Linux runtime also differs from the
Mac runtime used by these tiny tests, so compatibility is not assumed.

Next is a separately bounded Linux CPU qualification of this exact new source
bundle and tiny importer on an independently admitted runtime, including the
success and failure/cleanup cases. Preparing that run must bind the base
runtime, host-side helpers, new add-on and independent outer supervisor. This
stage did not create a workflow, submit CI or authorize reuse of an old attempt.
A GPU is not required for this tiny containment qualification.

Real-input mounts, existing 0600/private ownership rules, full-size memory and
output budgets, trusted metadata deserialization and the separately authorized
real import remain unresolved native boundaries. Then follow the outstanding
GPU worker/profile, private data relocation and CUDA/smoke prerequisites from
v0.70-v0.75. The saved real plan's caps are not increased by the tiny guard profile.
Gate 5, execution permission and production eligibility all remain false.

HEAD remains `ecc545fc423650bf1089311915290523c10b3172`. Tracked/staged diffs are
